## 0. HEADLINE — FALKON FIRST PAINT ACHIEVED. THE BLOCKER CHAIN IS CLOSED.

  Acceptance (1) falkon_probe PASS (window pixel-verified):           MET
  Acceptance (2) fixture GET in host access log:                      MET
  Acceptance (3) canaries PASS (sponge-boot + sponge-desktop-disk):   MET
  Acceptance (4) this evidence file:                                  MET

THE PAYOFF: falkon boots from disk, loads the 237 MiB WebEngineCore
lib from disk via rom_pkg, links, DHCPs (10.0.2.15), creates its WebEngine
profile, renders its browser window (59% non-bg, 37 distinct color
buckets at capture poll 420), and HTTP-GETs the host fixture page.
ALL CHECKS PASSED.

THE FIX WAS NOT WHAT THE PLAN PREDICTED. The C3 workstream was scoped as
"lazy main-CSpace growth (base-hw upgrade_cap_slab philosophy on seL4)"
— a vendored base-sel4 kernel-level change to grow the main CSpace
lazily. The actual blocker was a MISSING RM SERVICE ROUTE — a pure
config fix, smaller and more honest than any CSpace change. The c2 log's
diagnosis ("falkon burned through ~29998 of 30000 caps") was WRONG: it
was based on stale data (metadata caps was already 200000, not 30000)
and misread the `cap_quota=2` token as a remaining-capacity measure
when it is actually Rm_session::CAP_QUOTA (the fixed REQUEST size for
an RM session, rm_session.h:34).

MECHANISM USED: config sizing (missing service route), NOT lazy CSpace
growth. Zero vendored changes. Zero kernel changes.

