## 1. THE REAL BLOCKER — missing "RM" service route (not cap exhaustion)

### 1.1 The denial message, decoded

The C2 run2 failure (c2-sponge-falkon-disk-run2.log lines 707-709):

  [pkg_runtime] Warning: falkon: no route to service "RM" (label="falkon -> ")
  [falkon] Error: stop because parent denied RM-session: label="",
                 ram_quota=64K, cap_quota=2

Each token, traced to source (not speculated):

  "no route to service RM"
    -> sandbox/route_model.h:272-274. Printed when Route_model::resolve()
       exhausts ALL route rules + default-route targets without a match.
       The <parent/> target is only valid for services registered via
       <parent-provides> (sandbox/config_model.h Parent_provides_model;
       sandbox/library.cc:222-225 create_parent_service). RM was NOT in
       any parent-provides in the chain -> find_service throws
       Service_denied -> "no route" warning -> session DENIED.

  "ram_quota=64K"
    -> Rm_connection ctor (rm_session/connection.h:30): Ram_quota{64*1024}.
       This is the FIXED request size for an RM session, NOT a measure of
       remaining RAM.

  "cap_quota=2"
    -> Rm_session::CAP_QUOTA = 2 (rm_session/hm_session.h:34). This is the
       FIXED cap quota an Rm_connection requests, NOT a measure of
       remaining caps. The c2 log interpreted this as "only 2 caps remain"
       — that interpretation is WRONG.

  "stop because parent denied RM-session"
    -> base/src/lib/base/component.cc:200-201. The DENIED branch of the
       session-retry loop. falkon's Rm_connection request was denied by
       pkg_runtime (no route), and after the retry budget is exhausted,
       the component calls sleep_forever().

### 1.2 Why falkon needs RM (and why "RM (subsumed by PD)" is wrong)

The falkon metadata comment (pkg/falkon/metadata.xml, pre-fix) said:
  "RM (subsumed by PD)"

This is FACTUALLY INCORRECT. In Genode 26.05:
  - PD (pd_session.h) provides exactly THREE region maps: address_space()
    (line 238), stack_area() (line 243), linker_area() (line 248). These
    are the component's OWN address space, stack area, and linker area.
  - RM (rm_session.h) is a SEPARATE core service (base/src/core/main.cc:151
    Rm_root, :164 Core_service<Rm_session_component>) for creating
    ADDITIONAL region maps (sub-address-spaces).

WebEngine creates additional region maps at runtime via Rm_connection:
  - mmap (the libc mmap path for anonymous mappings uses Rm_session)
  - qtwebengine_shm (shared memory for WebEngine's render compositing)
  - WebEngine's internal heap region management

falkon completed ALL of init, WebEngineCore linking, AND DHCP (10.0.2.15)
using its initial PD-provided region maps. It only died when WebEngine's
runtime created its FIRST additional Rm_connection — and pkg_runtime had
no route for the "RM" service.

### 1.3 Why the main CSpace was NOT the problem

falkon's main CSpace has 32768 slots (C1: CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_1ST=6,
CSPACE_SIZE_LOG2_2ND=9, total 2^15=32768). falkon's cap_quota accounting
is 200000 (pkg/falkon/metadata.xml <quota caps="200000"/>). The binding
constraint is min(32768 slots, 200000 accounting) = 32768 slots.

From the C2 run2 log: falkon got through the ENTIRE init+link+DHCP
sequence WITHOUT any "out of selector" or cap-exhaustion message. The
ONLY failure was the RM route. This proves falkon's main-CSpace slot
consumption at the point of failure was well under 32768 — the CSpace
was NOT exhausted. The RM denial happened at a routing gate BEFORE any
cap/slot accounting was consulted.

