## 2. THE FIX — add "RM" to two parent-provides lists (3 Sponge-owned files)

### 2.1 The routing chain (4 hops, 2 were broken)

  falkon -> pkg_runtime -> system(nested init) -> Tier-0 init -> core

For RM to reach falkon, each hop must declare RM in its parent-provides:
  Hop 1: falkon's route catches RM via <any-service>-><parent/>
         (pkgd-generated, main.cc:1307). Works once pkg_runtime
         parent-provides has RM.                          [FIXED below]
  Hop 2: pkg_runtime's default-route catches RM via <any-service>->
         <parent/>|<any-child> (pkgd-generated, main.cc:1194-1199).
         Works once system parent-provides has RM.       [FIXED below]
  Hop 3: system's default-route catches RM via <any-service>->
         <parent/>|<any-child> (sponge-falkon-disk.run:382-386).
         Works once Tier-0 parent-provides has RM.       [already present]
  Hop 4: Tier-0 init parent-provides includes RM
         (sponge-falkon-disk.run:494).                   [already present]
         Core announces RM (main.cc:151,164).            [upstream]

The two broken hops were:
  - pkg_runtime parent-provides (generated by sponge_pkgd): missing RM
  - system.config parent-provides (in sponge-falkon-disk.run): missing RM

### 2.2 File 1: repos/sponge/src/sponge_pkgd/main.cc (pkgd generator)

Added "RM" to the hardcoded parent-provides list (after PD, before CPU),
with a comment documenting WHY (matching the existing Nic/Rtc comment
convention at the same site):

  g.node("service", [&] { g.attribute("name", "RM"); });

BLAST RADIUS: affects ALL scenarios using sponge_pkgd (terminal, textedit,
files, falkon, launch, pkg-gui, pkg-lifecycle, desktop-disk). Adding RM
to parent-provides is HARMLESS for packages that don't request RM — it
just declares the service as available from the parent. Only falkon
(WebEngine) actually constructs Rm_connections; the others never exercise
the route. Verified: sponge-desktop-disk PASS (alpha-probe PASS) with
the change.

### 2.3 File 2: run/sponge-falkon-disk.run (system.config parent-provides)

Added "+ service RM" to the nested system init's parent-provides (after
PD, matching the sponge-desktop-disk.run pattern at line 541):

  + parent-provides
    + service ROM
    + service PD
    + service RM          <- ADDED
    + service CPU
    ...

This was an OMISSION unique to sponge-falkon-disk.run — sponge-desktop-
disk.run already had RM (line 541). The falkon-disk system.config was
written without it because the metadata comment "RM (subsumed by PD)"
led the author to believe it wasn't needed.

### 2.4 File 3: pkg/falkon/metadata.xml (comment correction)

Corrected the factually wrong "RM (subsumed by PD)" comment in the
<sessions> section to accurately state that RM is a distinct core
service, not subsumed by PD, and is handled by sponge_pkgd's parent-
provides (no per-package <session> route needed). Per AGENTS.md
"Documentation Matches Code."

### 2.5 What was NOT changed

  - genode/repos/base-sel4/** : UNTOUCHED (zero vendored changes)
  - capability_space_sel4.h   : UNTOUCHED (C1's 32768-slot config holds)
  - vm_space.h                : UNTOUCHED (C2's lazy config holds)
  - No lazy main-CSpace growth was needed or implemented.

