## 5. Correction of the prior diagnosis chain

The blocker progression across the three workstreams, as ACTUALLY
observed (not as predicted):

  C1 (commit 93ded092f1): size-aware CNode backing -> main CSpace 32768
    slots. NEEDED and CORRECT — falkon's main CSpace was previously
    hard-capped at 8192 (upstream), which WAS a real limit. C1's 32768
    is sufficient for falkon's actual main-CSpace consumption (verified:
    falkon reached first paint at 32768 slots with no "out of selector").

  C2 (commit 19303468ff): lazy vm_space growth -> 131072 mappings/PD.
    NEEDED and CORRECT — the "out of selector" / "mapping cache full"
    blocker was a real vm_space limit. C2's 131072 selectors handle
    falkon's ~100k page-frame mappings and rom_pkg's ~130k.

  C3 (THIS WORKSTREAM): the predicted "main-CSpace cap quota exhaustion"
    did NOT exist. The actual blocker was a missing RM service route.
    Fixed with a 3-line config change (add RM to two parent-provides
    lists + correct one comment). No CSpace change needed.

The c2-lazy-vmspace.log §3 diagnosis was based on two errors:
  (a) Stale caps value: it cited "falkon's init-donated cap quota is
      30000" — the metadata was already 200000 (raised in P4).
  (b) Misread cap_quota=2: it interpreted this as "only 2 caps remain"
      — actually Rm_session::CAP_QUOTA (the fixed request size).

Both errors are corrected here. The fix validates that C1's 32768-slot
main CSpace and C2's 131072-selector vm_space are BOTH correctly sized
for falkon's workload.

